---
import "@fontsource-variable/public-sans/wght.css";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Grant Wasil builds software and helps people use AI to make their lives better. Selected projects and systems work." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://grantwasil.com/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Grant Wasil" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="I build software and help people use AI to make their lives better." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://grantwasil.com/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Grant Wasil</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="identity"><span class="logo" aria-hidden="true"></span><h1>Grant Wasil</h1></header>
      <p class="lead">I build software and help people use AI to make their lives better.</p>
      <p>At Gary Community Ventures, I work with people to figure out where AI can genuinely help. Sometimes that means building a tool. Sometimes it means rethinking a workflow or sitting down together to try something out. I do the engineering and the coaching, and I run demos and office hours where people can bring their own questions.</p>
      <p>Before Gary, I was a site reliability engineer at Duo Security / Cisco.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Contact and profiles">
        <a href="mailto:dev@grantwasil.com">Email</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/GrantWasil">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/grant-wasil/">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://x.com/GrantWasil">X</a>
      </nav>

      <section aria-labelledby="work">
        <h2 id="work">Some work</h2>
        <article>
          <div class="paintr-layout">
            <div class="paintr-story">
              <h3><a href="https://paintr.dev">paintr</a></h3>
              <p>An iPhone and iPad app that turns your own photos into paint-by-number puzzles.</p>
              <p>I built paintr for my wife, who loves settling into long, detailed painting sessions. That shaped the app: choose how much detail you want, take your time, and come back to a painting over several evenings.</p>
              <p>Photos are converted on your device. You can also share a puzzle with someone so they can paint their own copy, with the option to keep the finished picture a surprise.</p>
              <p class="links"><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/paintr-a-little-color/id6808892551">App Store</a> · <a href="https://paintr.dev">Website</a></p>
            </div>
            <details id="paintr-screenshot" class="painting-disclosure" open>
              <summary><span class="when-closed">View screenshot</span><span class="when-open">Hide screenshot</span></summary>
              <a class="painting-link" href="/assets/paintr-iphone-painting.webp" aria-label="View full-size screenshot of paintr on iPhone">
              <figure class="painting">
                <img src="/assets/paintr-iphone-painting.webp" width="1206" height="2622" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="paintr on iPhone showing The sunniest seat, a partly painted orange cat, outlined unpainted regions, and numbered color pots." />
                <figcaption>A painting in progress in paintr on iPhone.<span class="full-size-label">View full-size</span></figcaption>
              </figure>
              </a>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="https://github.com/GrantWasil/VideoPaste">VideoPaste</a></h3>
          <p>A Mac app and browser extensions I built to copy videos from supported Reddit and public X posts directly to your clipboard, ready to paste into a chat.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="https://github.com/GrantWasil/crewview">crewview</a></h3>
          <p>A tool I built to delegate work from Codex to Claude and keep track of the resulting jobs and conversations.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>AWS rollout automation at Duo Security / Cisco</h3>
          <p>I automated a recurring operating-system patch rollout so it could begin when new hardened images became available. The system rolled changes through AWS infrastructure in stages, using service health checks and time between stages to catch failures.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <p class="personal">I’m based in Colorado. Outside of work, I’m usually bringing people together around a game, an escape room, or a murder mystery party. I like creating things people can participate in, whether that’s an app, a workshop, or a slightly overambitious game night.</p>
      <p class="contact"><a href="mailto:dev@grantwasil.com">Email</a></p>
    </main>
    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        const disclosure = document.getElementById("paintr-screenshot");
        const trigger = disclosure.querySelector("summary");
        const mobile = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 600px)");
        const imageLink = document.querySelector(".painting-link");
        const savedPainting = history.state?.paintrScreenshot;
        const returningToPainting = savedPainting && performance.getEntriesByType("navigation")[0]?.type === "back_forward";
        let mobileOpen = returningToPainting ? savedPainting.open : false;
        let wasMobile = mobile.matches;
        const applyLayout = () => {
          if (wasMobile && !mobile.matches) mobileOpen = disclosure.open;
          disclosure.open = mobile.matches ? mobileOpen : true;
          if (!mobile.matches && document.activeElement === trigger) {
            document.querySelector(".paintr-story h3 a").focus({ preventScroll: true });
          }
          wasMobile = mobile.matches;
        };
        disclosure.addEventListener("toggle", () => {
          if (wasMobile && mobile.matches) mobileOpen = disclosure.open;
        });
        mobile.addEventListener("change", applyLayout);
        imageLink.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
          if (event.button === 0 && !event.metaKey && !event.ctrlKey && !event.shiftKey && !event.altKey) {
            history.replaceState({ ...history.state, paintrScreenshot: { open: disclosure.open } }, "");
          }
        });
        window.addEventListener("pageshow", (event) => {
          if ((event.persisted || returningToPainting) && history.state?.paintrScreenshot) {
            imageLink.focus({ preventScroll: true });
            const restoredState = { ...history.state };
            delete restoredState.paintrScreenshot;
            history.replaceState(restoredState, "");
          }
        });
        applyLayout();
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  :global(:root) { color-scheme: light dark; --page: #fff; --ink: #252525; --secondary: #505050; --link: #245399; --link-hover: #153466; --selection: #dce8fa; }
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; background: var(--page); color: var(--ink); font-family: "Public Sans Variable", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; }
  :global(::selection) { background: var(--selection); color: var(--ink); }
  main { max-width: 690px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 28px 72px; }
  .identity { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .logo { display: block; width: 60px; height: 36px; flex: 0 0 60px; background-color: currentColor; -webkit-mask: url("/gwlogo.png") -29px -23px / 112px auto no-repeat; mask: url("/gwlogo.png") -29px -23px / 112px auto no-repeat; }
  h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  h2 { margin: 32px 0 16px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.4; }
  h3 { display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; margin: 0 0 5px; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.5; }
  p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lead { margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
  a { color: var(--link); text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  a:hover { color: var(--link-hover); }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: 1px; }
  nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; column-gap: 18px; row-gap: 8px; }
  nav a, h3 a, .links a, .contact a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-width: 44px; min-height: 44px; }
  article + article { margin-top: 26px; }
  article p { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .paintr-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 180px; gap: 28px; align-items: start; }
  .paintr-story { min-width: 0; }
  .paintr-story p { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .paintr-story .links { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .painting-disclosure > summary { display: none; color: var(--link); cursor: pointer; min-height: 44px; line-height: 44px; list-style-position: inside; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }
  .painting-disclosure > summary:hover { color: var(--link-hover); }
  .painting-disclosure > summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: 1px; }
  .painting-disclosure > summary span { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  .painting-disclosure .when-open, .painting-disclosure[open] .when-closed { display: none; }
  .painting-disclosure[open] .when-open { display: inline; }
  .painting { width: 100%; max-width: 300px; margin: 0; }
  .painting-link { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 300px; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .painting-link:hover { color: inherit; }
  .full-size-label { display: block; color: var(--link); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .painting-link:hover .full-size-label { color: var(--link-hover); }
  .painting img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 4px; }
  .painting figcaption { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--secondary); }
  .links { font-size: 14px; }
  .personal { margin-top: 36px; color: var(--secondary); }
  .contact { margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :global(:root) { --page: #181818; --ink: #fff; --secondary: #d6d6d6; --link: #9bc2ff; --link-hover: #c9deff; --selection: #345078; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .paintr-layout { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; } .painting-link { margin-inline: auto; } .painting-disclosure > summary { display: list-item; } .painting-disclosure[open] .painting-link { margin-top: 16px; } }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { main { padding: 36px 22px 48px; } }
</style>
